

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------
# Commit message template. Lines that start with "#" are ignored.
# Enable it once per clone:  git config commit.template .gitmessage
#
# Format:
#
#   <type>(<scope>): <summary>
#
#   <body>
#
#   <trailers>
#
# Subject line
#   - Use the imperative mood: "add", not "added" or "adds".
#   - Use 72 characters or fewer. Do not end with a period.
#   - Types:  feat, fix, docs, test, refactor, perf, build, ci, chore,
#             revert
#   - Scopes: dsl, gen, trace, cli, nextjs, react, fastapi, examples,
#             repo, deps. Omit the scope if the change has no one area.
#   - Breaking change: put "!" before the colon, for example
#     "feat(dsl)!: rename entity fields to attributes".
#
# Body (optional, one blank line after the subject)
#   - Say what changes and why. The diff shows how.
#   - Wrap lines at 72 characters.
#
# Trailers (one blank line after the body)
#   Refs #<issue>                  the story that the commit is part of
#   Closes #<issue>                only if the commit completes the story
#   BREAKING CHANGE: <description> if the subject has "!"
#   Co-Authored-By: <name> <email> for paired or AI-assisted work
#
# Do not put links to claude.ai in commit messages.
# See CONTRIBUTING.md, section "Commits".
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------
